  "implementation": [
    "Original IrisGeneratorStyle hash/prefix/source stamp/stale-pruning control flow executes; active-prefix metadata is owned by the snapshot.",
    "Build-time original GenerationKernelRegistry current kernel identity is captured and checked against the actual revision-resource SHA-256. Browser cache fingerprint initialization uses that captured string; this does not qualify the native build or enable saved-world history.",
    "Original CNG.cached numerical fill loop, float casts, FloatCache input/output codecs, coordinate bounds and uncached/1D/3D behavior remain unchanged.",
    "Only File allocation, streams, directory listing/deletion and atomic move calls in the native cache paths bind to a snapshot-owned memory store. No files are persisted, imported from .cache or written to packs/worlds.",
    "Per snapshot: maximum 1024-square tiles, 8 MiB stored serialized bytes, 64 serialized files, 128 prefix keys/admitted tile keys and 64 MiB cumulative estimated allocation work. Admission charges 4096+16*size*size on every CNG cache invocation, including disk-equivalent reloads. This is not a measured heap guarantee.",
    "Cached styles and nested snippets trigger native pack-snapshot capture; cache-only styles are discoverable with the native FLAT default. Legacy non-native lowering refuses cached styles with the native-path guidance.",
    "noiseCacheStatistics and inspectNoiseCache expose counts/budgets/reload activity and encoded tile names/lengths/SHA-256. Scalar worker results include cache statistics and captured native identity. Snapshot clear/release removes serialized tiles, admission and prefix metadata.",
    "Cache bounds, expired-owner and IO boundary failures retain an Error cause; original GenerationFailures classifies them as engine failures so caught content loops must abort rather than silently omit a cache-backed layer."
  ],
